WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.040 --> 00:00:07.920
It seems like half of the comments think this
movie is an Abe Sapien origin story from the

00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:11.551
Hellboy universe and the other half think
we're dealing with the Creature from the Black

00:00:11.551 --> 00:00:12.551
Lagoon.

00:00:12.551 --> 00:00:16.130
Throughout this video, I'll be presenting
the evidence for both these theories, so stay

00:00:16.130 --> 00:00:19.710
to the end, where I'll give you my answer
on what this film actually is.

00:00:19.710 --> 00:00:23.631
Early on, we've got some surreal imagery of
furniture floating in an underwater room,

00:00:23.631 --> 00:00:24.631
but if you look closely you'll see that it's
not just the room that's underwater, but there

00:00:24.631 --> 00:00:27.100
some fish swimming by outside that window
as well.

00:00:27.100 --> 00:00:31.380
My prediction is that these shots are part
of a dream sequence because generally in my

00:00:31.380 --> 00:00:35.460
experience, desk lamps don't work underwater,
they just end up electrocuting the victim.

00:00:35.460 --> 00:00:36.970
I mean... uh... forget I said that.

00:00:36.970 --> 00:00:41.050
But even if lamps did work underwater, they'd
probably have to be plugged in.

00:00:41.050 --> 00:00:44.340
In the corner of the frame here, you see what
appears to be a tentacle, something we've

00:00:44.340 --> 00:00:48.730
seen plenty of in the Hellboy movies, whereas
Creature from the Black lagoon is much more

00:00:48.730 --> 00:00:49.930
grounded in reality.

00:00:49.930 --> 00:00:54.790
Side note: I love how they put their Fox Searchlight
logo underwater, it reminds me of the 30th

00:00:54.790 --> 00:00:56.640
Century Fox thing they used in Futurama.

00:00:56.640 --> 00:01:00.060
Her waking up here supports my theory that
the shots in the beginning of the trailer

00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:04.049
are part of a dream, and she's also in the
same room as that underwater part, so I'm

00:01:04.049 --> 00:01:07.860
pretty sure this scene represents her waking
up into the harsh reality of her real world

00:01:07.860 --> 00:01:08.940
responsibilities.

00:01:08.940 --> 00:01:12.640
Also, time seems to be a major theme in this
movie.

00:01:12.640 --> 00:01:16.830
You'll see over and over and over in this
trailer that the tracking of time seems to

00:01:16.830 --> 00:01:17.850
be important.

00:01:17.850 --> 00:01:22.130
This could be due to the fact that fish people
in fiction tend to live much longer than humans,

00:01:22.130 --> 00:01:25.900
which is a weird consistency when you think
about it considering how short lifespans tend

00:01:25.900 --> 00:01:27.690
to be for actual fish.

00:01:27.690 --> 00:01:31.801
One example of a fictional fish-person with
an extended lifespan, you guessed it: Abe

00:01:31.801 --> 00:01:33.549
Sapien from Hellboy.

00:01:33.549 --> 00:01:37.280
The Hellboy movies seem to take place in the
year they were released, as suggested by a

00:01:37.280 --> 00:01:40.280
reference to the recent advent of YouTube
in the second film.

00:01:40.280 --> 00:01:42.420
"They put them up on YouTube.

00:01:42.420 --> 00:01:43.850
God, I hate YouTube."

00:01:43.850 --> 00:01:47.180
Abe is stated to have been discovered alive
in 1865.

00:01:47.180 --> 00:01:51.590
That makes him at least 139 years old during
the first Hellboy movie.

00:01:51.590 --> 00:01:55.420
So perhaps the constant references to time
in the trailer play into the theme that the

00:01:55.420 --> 00:02:00.000
protagonist, Elisa, really has a limited time
with this fish-person, whatever he may turn

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:01.909
out to be, in the grand scheme of things.

00:02:01.909 --> 00:02:05.860
I've seen romantic complications caused by
a difference in the speed of aging in other

00:02:05.860 --> 00:02:10.189
stories before, so I wouldn't be surprised
if that was a big part of The Shape of Water

00:02:10.189 --> 00:02:11.189
as well.

00:02:11.189 --> 00:02:13.109
I guess only time will tell.

00:02:13.109 --> 00:02:15.090
Haha, oh I am just not funny.

00:02:15.090 --> 00:02:19.379
According to the internet, the movie takes
place in 1963 and has some connections to

00:02:19.379 --> 00:02:24.999
the Cold War, however, I think this part of
the film must start a bit earlier in 1962,

00:02:24.999 --> 00:02:30.319
and maybe it carries over into '63, because
this date, September 18th, falls on a Wednesday

00:02:30.319 --> 00:02:32.799
in '63, but a Tuesday in '62.

00:02:32.799 --> 00:02:37.269
I looked up the date in 1962 and apparently
some nuclear testing was performed by the

00:02:37.269 --> 00:02:38.840
USSR that day.

00:02:38.840 --> 00:02:43.269
In an interview earlier this year, Doug Jones,
who by the way is the same actor who played

00:02:43.269 --> 00:02:47.459
Abe Sapien in Del Toro's Hellboy films, said
the following about his role in The Shape

00:02:47.459 --> 00:02:48.459
of Water:

00:02:48.459 --> 00:02:53.779
"I'm being studied and tested in a U.S. government
facility in 1963, so the Russian Cold War

00:02:53.779 --> 00:02:57.980
is on, the race for space is on, so there's
all that backdrop and that undercurrent.

00:02:57.980 --> 00:03:02.250
I'm being tested for how can they use me for
advantages in military or space travel, or

00:03:02.250 --> 00:03:04.829
my technology-can we make this usable for
humans?

00:03:04.829 --> 00:03:07.449
So they're trying to keep me a secret from
the Russians."

00:03:07.449 --> 00:03:11.189
So that leads me to believe that the The Shape
of Water is about the US is developing this

00:03:11.189 --> 00:03:16.739
supernatural research program to as a reaction,
to try to outpace the USSR in the Cold War.

00:03:16.739 --> 00:03:20.830
Whether or not that turns out to be the Bureau
for Paranormal Research and Defense, Section

00:03:20.830 --> 00:03:24.230
51, from the Hellboy franchise, remains to
be seen.

00:03:24.230 --> 00:03:28.959
Moving on, this wallpaper, reminds me a lot
of the carpet in Room 237 in The Shining.

00:03:28.959 --> 00:03:33.589
That's probably just a coincidence, or at
most an homage, but it did get my attention

00:03:33.589 --> 00:03:36.840
enough to take a closer look at it and notice
that it also looks kind of like fish scales.

00:03:36.840 --> 00:03:41.249
It's shown again at the end of the trailer
and it really starts to look fishy.

00:03:41.249 --> 00:03:43.750
There's something special about these shoes
that they keep showing.

00:03:43.750 --> 00:03:48.019
I'm not entirely sure what it is yet, but
go ahead and leave your ideas in the comments,

00:03:48.019 --> 00:03:51.340
and if I do a follow-up video, I'll put your
comment up on the screen.

00:03:51.340 --> 00:03:55.530
She cleans these shoes with an oddly specific
duck brush thing.

00:03:55.530 --> 00:03:58.919
And overall she seems to be obsessed with
cleaning, because in addition to keeping her

00:03:58.919 --> 00:04:02.260
own things things, she also does it for a
living.

00:04:02.260 --> 00:04:04.109
Webbed fingers.

00:04:04.109 --> 00:04:08.569
That could support the idea of either Hellboy
or Black Lagoon, but again, I'd have to lean

00:04:08.569 --> 00:04:09.879
more towards Hellboy.

00:04:09.879 --> 00:04:13.449
The hand looks more humanoid than the hands
of the Creature, which are much wider and

00:04:13.449 --> 00:04:14.519
more claw like.

00:04:14.519 --> 00:04:18.329
That's not to say that if this was related
to Creature of the Black Lagoon that Del Toro

00:04:18.329 --> 00:04:20.090
wouldn't have updated the design a bit.

00:04:20.090 --> 00:04:24.280
It has been over 60 years since the movie
came out, and to be fair it's also been 9

00:04:24.280 --> 00:04:28.260
years since the last time Abe Sapien showed
up on screen, so it's possible we'd see a

00:04:28.260 --> 00:04:30.010
fresh look there as well.

00:04:30.010 --> 00:04:34.350
In this shot, a warning on the wall reads
"NO LONE ZONE", which I guess means that no

00:04:34.350 --> 00:04:36.370
one should ever be in there unsupervised.

00:04:36.370 --> 00:04:39.230
Kind of like she is right here.

00:04:39.230 --> 00:04:43.280
Also, if you don't know what these are, it's
a security measure meant to reinforce that

00:04:43.280 --> 00:04:44.500
"no lone zone" rule.

00:04:44.500 --> 00:04:48.760
The door only opens if both buttons are pressed
at the same time, so you need two people to

00:04:48.760 --> 00:04:49.760
do it.

00:04:49.760 --> 00:04:53.500
If you are a Hellboy fan, you probably didn't
miss this one: eggs!

00:04:53.500 --> 00:04:57.010
Abe Sapien loves eggs, so that's a huge connection.

00:04:57.010 --> 00:04:59.710
However, you'll notice that the eyes...

00:04:59.710 --> 00:05:03.040
wait a minute... where have I seen this before?

00:05:03.040 --> 00:05:09.240
But anyway, you'll notice the eyes are not
quite the same as Abe's, but do keep in mind

00:05:09.240 --> 00:05:13.260
that he can change the appearance of his eyes
using those contacts that he wears, even though

00:05:13.260 --> 00:05:15.370
you're not supposed to wear your contacts
underwater.

00:05:15.370 --> 00:05:20.030
Also, the creatures in that franchise do change
their appearance with age just like anyone

00:05:20.030 --> 00:05:21.030
else.

00:05:21.030 --> 00:05:24.370
This chain gives the impression that this
creature might be dangerous, which would be

00:05:24.370 --> 00:05:26.080
a tally for Black Lagoon.

00:05:26.080 --> 00:05:27.980
Abe Sapien is not much of combatant.

00:05:27.980 --> 00:05:31.660
He only get into one scrum during the series,
which he runs away from.

00:05:31.660 --> 00:05:36.130
The Creature from the Black Lagoon is confrontational,
has the power to rock the boat, literally,

00:05:36.130 --> 00:05:38.590
and breaks out of a cage with thick wooden
bars.

00:05:38.590 --> 00:05:42.960
Also, this guy's hand is wrapped up, so it's
likely that he was attacked by said creature.

00:05:42.960 --> 00:05:46.990
The obvious rebuttal is that if this creature
is so dangerous, why is it going and falling

00:05:46.990 --> 00:05:48.050
in love with Amelie...

00:05:48.050 --> 00:05:49.490
I mean, Elisa.

00:05:49.490 --> 00:05:52.900
Well, Doug Jones says that this creature is
the last of it's kind.

00:05:52.900 --> 00:05:55.030
That doesn't mean it was always that way.

00:05:55.030 --> 00:05:58.990
So maybe this isn't the same creature from
the black lagoon, but a descendant.

00:05:58.990 --> 00:06:03.060
If the descendant was brought up under different
conditions, maybe it's less hostile.

00:06:03.060 --> 00:06:06.430
And let's not forgot that in The Creature
From The Black Lagoon, all of the men who

00:06:06.430 --> 00:06:10.990
are caught off guard get killed, but Kay,
the one female of the group, leaves herself

00:06:10.990 --> 00:06:15.150
vulnerable, but the creature just touches
her legs, and then at the end, (spoiler alert

00:06:15.150 --> 00:06:21.520
for Creature from the Black Lagoon) kidnaps
her but does not kill her.

00:06:21.520 --> 00:06:24.890
Maybe Lagoon Creatures need love too.

00:06:24.890 --> 00:06:29.360
Back to the trailer, this scientist guy claims
that the creature is intelligent, capable

00:06:29.360 --> 00:06:32.420
of language and understanding emotions.

00:06:32.420 --> 00:06:34.490
Both Abe and the Creature are intelligent.

00:06:34.490 --> 00:06:38.580
Abe reads four books a day and is able to
extract information from people he meets.

00:06:38.580 --> 00:06:43.210
The Creature devises a plan to trap the boat
inside the lagoon using a huge tree branch.

00:06:43.210 --> 00:06:46.400
Abe demonstrates the ability to use language,
which the creature does not.

00:06:46.400 --> 00:06:49.440
That doesn't mean it's impossible, it just
doesn't happen during the movie.

00:06:49.440 --> 00:06:52.740
I would argue that both are capable of understanding
emotion.

00:06:52.740 --> 00:06:56.460
Abe falls in love during the second movie,
which leads to a glorious scene involving

00:06:56.460 --> 00:06:59.220
two supernatural monsters singing a love song.

00:06:59.220 --> 00:07:05.050
The Creature expresses both anger and love;
anger when he retaliates at them for shooting

00:07:05.050 --> 00:07:07.960
at him and love, as I mentioned earlier, towards
Kay.

00:07:07.960 --> 00:07:11.360
In the Shape of Water trailer, Elisa plays
some music for the fish-man.

00:07:11.360 --> 00:07:16.030
She offers him up some jazz music, maybe that's
not his thing, they settle on classical music.

00:07:16.030 --> 00:07:19.670
Or at least, something in the style of classical
music.

00:07:19.670 --> 00:07:22.940
The artist of this track is actually Madeleine
Peyroux.

00:07:22.940 --> 00:07:28.340
She was born in 1974, over a decade after
this movie is supposed to take place.

00:07:28.340 --> 00:07:32.400
So that doesn't really make sense, it seems
Guillermo Del Toro is pulling a Baz Luhrmann

00:07:32.400 --> 00:07:35.510
in this instance and using music from the
wrong era.

00:07:35.510 --> 00:07:39.350
But the point is, that this track, which features
instrumentals you might hear in classical

00:07:39.350 --> 00:07:44.690
music is what makes this creature dance, and
Abe Sapien is also a fan of such music.

00:07:44.690 --> 00:07:48.720
If you are curious about the song itself,
it's called La Ja-vanaise, and the lyrics

00:07:48.720 --> 00:07:50.560
translate roughly as follows:

00:07:50.560 --> 00:07:54.280
"I admit I went through hell, didn’t you
my love?

00:07:54.280 --> 00:07:57.370
Before I caught wind of you (met you) my love.

00:07:57.370 --> 00:08:00.660
Whether it pleases you or not
In dancing the Javanaise,

00:08:00.660 --> 00:08:03.750
We loved each other for the length of a song."

00:08:03.750 --> 00:08:07.500
That last line could tie back into the time
thing I mentioned earlier; because he lives

00:08:07.500 --> 00:08:11.100
much longer than her, it may feel like their
love was short lived to him.

00:08:11.100 --> 00:08:15.270
We also know Abe is a sucker for poetry and
love songs, and this may be the origin of

00:08:15.270 --> 00:08:16.970
why those things resonate with him.

00:08:16.970 --> 00:08:17.970
Next thing.

00:08:17.970 --> 00:08:21.020
"The natives of the Amazon worshipped him."

00:08:21.020 --> 00:08:24.180
Well, the Black Lagoon is located in the Amazon.

00:08:24.180 --> 00:08:28.510
Abe on the other hand was found in Washington,
but we don't know where was located before

00:08:28.510 --> 00:08:32.940
that, or if the Amazonian natives worshipped
a different member of his species back in

00:08:32.940 --> 00:08:35.610
the day, before he became the last remaining
member.

00:08:35.610 --> 00:08:39.620
This seems to be the same room as Elisa's
apartment from the beginning of the trailer.

00:08:39.620 --> 00:08:41.599
Over here we see a drawing board.

00:08:41.599 --> 00:08:47.110
Later in the trailer, when we see this rendering,
we know that Elisa is most likely the artist.

00:08:47.110 --> 00:08:51.079
There's also a self portrait of her peaking
around a corner, possibly foreshadowing the

00:08:51.079 --> 00:08:53.620
fact that she'll be sneaking around later
in the movie.

00:08:53.620 --> 00:08:56.360
Like in this next shot of the trailer.

00:08:56.360 --> 00:08:59.820
Calling it now: I think this scene is part
of the dream too.

00:08:59.820 --> 00:09:03.839
Outside the movie theater, if you look behind
the staircase, we can make out part of a word.

00:09:03.839 --> 00:09:07.529
Being that it is a cinema, it probably says
"feature" or "featured".

00:09:07.529 --> 00:09:11.499
But I was thinking, what if it says "creature",
or even "creature feature".

00:09:11.499 --> 00:09:15.589
That could explain why the creature is the
only one interested in seeing this movie.

00:09:15.589 --> 00:09:19.839
Perhaps there's a jealousy subplot where the
creature longs for someone of it's own kind.

00:09:19.839 --> 00:09:22.990
By the way if you can figure out what movie
this is, let me know in the comments.

00:09:22.990 --> 00:09:27.089
The bloody handprint here doesn't look like
a normal human hand, so I'm gonna guess that

00:09:27.089 --> 00:09:31.079
is also the creature, meaning he probably
escaped and got himself into some trouble.

00:09:31.079 --> 00:09:34.939
This guy is asleep, so he won't be much help
as a witness of this crime.

00:09:34.939 --> 00:09:38.899
Based on this license plate, it looks like
the movie takes place in Maryland, possibly

00:09:38.899 --> 00:09:39.899
Massachusetts.

00:09:39.899 --> 00:09:42.920
If you're wondering where Hellboy is set,
it's in New Jersey.

00:09:42.920 --> 00:09:47.300
And if you aren't familiar with American geography,
all of those locations are set in the Northeast

00:09:47.300 --> 00:09:49.569
region, not too far away from one another.

00:09:49.569 --> 00:09:53.872
While Black Lagoon was set in the Amazon,
much of that crew was American, so it would

00:09:53.872 --> 00:09:56.759
make sense that they might capture something
and bring it back with them.

00:09:56.759 --> 00:10:00.600
I don't know who's bath this is, but this
container on the side stuck out to me.

00:10:00.600 --> 00:10:05.589
It's labeled: Aviex, a company that develops
vaccines to combat parasitic diseases.

00:10:05.589 --> 00:10:08.800
Definitely a strange item to have laying around
the bathroom.

00:10:08.800 --> 00:10:12.600
Now I could be wrong about this one, but I
think the voice at the beginning and end of

00:10:12.600 --> 00:10:14.649
the trailer is Doug Jones.

00:10:14.649 --> 00:10:18.629
Obviously that's significant because he played
Abe Sapien, but that doesn't confirm that

00:10:18.629 --> 00:10:22.809
The Shape of Water is a hellboy spin-off,
because director Guillermo Del Toro likes

00:10:22.809 --> 00:10:27.160
to work with the same actors over and over
again, just as many directors do as part of

00:10:27.160 --> 00:10:30.029
their auteur, part of their directorial style.

00:10:30.029 --> 00:10:35.689
The reason that it would be significant if
that was indeed his voice is; A) he talks;

00:10:35.689 --> 00:10:40.640
and B) he refers to Elisa as the princess
without voice, and if you've seen Hellboy

00:10:40.640 --> 00:10:43.740
II, you know he kind of has a thing for princesses.

00:10:43.740 --> 00:10:48.869
I'm not saying that Elisa is literally a princess,
but he likes calling a girl princess, so that's

00:10:48.869 --> 00:10:51.529
more evidence that these movies are connected.

00:10:51.529 --> 00:10:56.129
So now you have a good argument for this movie
being connected to either the Hellboy or Creature

00:10:56.129 --> 00:10:57.829
of the Black Lagoon franchises.

00:10:57.829 --> 00:11:01.620
I think there is quite a bit more support
for the Abe Sapien idea, but I have seen an

00:11:01.620 --> 00:11:05.560
article online that basically shoots down
the possibility, saying that fans are trying

00:11:05.560 --> 00:11:09.570
too hard to connect the dots, much as many
of my commenters have said about these trailer

00:11:09.570 --> 00:11:10.889
analysis videos.

00:11:10.889 --> 00:11:14.819
The article also brings up that Del Toro legally
wouldn't be able to make such a film due to

00:11:14.819 --> 00:11:17.610
a reboot of the franchise already being in
development.

00:11:17.610 --> 00:11:20.499
But how to do we know that Del Toro isn't
involved in the reboot?

00:11:20.499 --> 00:11:22.550
How do we know this movie isn't a part of
it?

00:11:22.550 --> 00:11:26.930
Creature of the Black Lagoon is also being
remade in 2019, but nobody's arguing against

00:11:26.930 --> 00:11:28.309
the possibility of that.

00:11:28.309 --> 00:11:31.249
You have a fish person who likes eggs and
vintage music.

00:11:31.249 --> 00:11:34.899
There's no proof that this one has telepathic
abilities, but he clearly has a connection

00:11:34.899 --> 00:11:37.199
with a girl who is mute, she can't speak.

00:11:37.199 --> 00:11:41.279
"When he looks at me, he does not know how
I am incomplete."

00:11:41.279 --> 00:11:44.320
He's able to understand her despite the fact
that she can't talk.

00:11:44.320 --> 00:11:49.019
In 2002, before any of the Hellboy stuff came
out, Del Toro was briefly attached to a remake

00:11:49.019 --> 00:11:53.809
of Creature from the Black Lagoon, so I think
he's just a fan of it, he's inspired by it,

00:11:53.809 --> 00:11:55.069
and that's why we see these similarities.

00:11:55.069 --> 00:11:59.600
There was also an article recently where Mr.
Del Toro flat out denies the existence of

00:11:59.600 --> 00:12:00.959
Hellboy III.

00:12:00.959 --> 00:12:03.839
Does this mean that Shape of Water can't be
a Hellboy spin-off?

00:12:03.839 --> 00:12:05.199
Not exactly.

00:12:05.199 --> 00:12:09.050
I'm going to spoil the end of M Night Shyamalan's
Split right, so if you haven't seen that,

00:12:09.050 --> 00:12:13.870
then skip ahead like 20 seconds, but I think
what GDT is doing here is creating doubt to

00:12:13.870 --> 00:12:14.870
create surprise.

00:12:14.870 --> 00:12:19.269
I remember shortly before Split came out,
Shyamalan responded to a tweet asking about

00:12:19.269 --> 00:12:20.809
a sequel to Unbreakable.

00:12:20.809 --> 00:12:24.360
He said that he had a script sitting on his
kitchen counter and created the expectation

00:12:24.360 --> 00:12:27.279
that this might be something that happens
a few years down the road.

00:12:27.279 --> 00:12:31.029
Then just a few months after that, we got
Split and it was a delightful surprise.

00:12:31.029 --> 00:12:33.699
I see The Shape Of Water kind of playing out
the same way.

00:12:33.699 --> 00:12:36.819
I don't think it will be heavy handed with
the Hellboy references, I think it will be

00:12:36.819 --> 00:12:39.670
it's own movie that happens to work in this
universe.

00:12:39.670 --> 00:12:42.509
Kind of like Split last year, kind of like
10 Cloverfield Lane.

00:12:42.509 --> 00:12:45.500
So that's what I believe, I'm gonna put my
eggs in that basket.

00:12:45.500 --> 00:12:46.500
Pun intended.

